  "extraction": "Single row extracted verbatim from erass1_emain_raw.tsv by numerical coordinate match. No value altered. Raw catalogue kept alongside as erass1_emain_raw.tsv.",
  "note": "MACS J0416.1-2403. Instrument: eROSITA (eRASS1 survey, 142.9 s exposure). *** GLOBAL / INTEGRATED QUANTITIES ONLY - THERE IS NO RADIAL PROFILE IN THIS CATALOGUE *** eRASS1 emain is a detection catalogue: it reports count rates, fluxes and luminosities inside fixed apertures (300 kpc and R500), not n_e(r) or T(r). *** THE TEMPERATURE IS UNUSABLE ***: the KT column is EMPTY for this cluster; only a lower bound b_KT = 2.38 keV is given, with no upper bound. With 144.2 counts in R500 from a 142.9 s survey exposure, eROSITA cannot constrain the temperature here. The Chandra global kT = 10.06 keV from Ogrean et al. 2015 (macsj0416_ogrean2015_global_properties.tsv) is far superior and should be preferred. Identity confirmed by the catalogue's own MatchName column, which cross-identifies this detection with ACTDR5 ACT-CL J0416.1-2404; zBest=0.3994 (spec) vs the literature z=0.396. Apertures are full circles - NO core excision. DERIVED COLUMNS: Mgas500 is inferred from the count rate assuming an emission profile shape; M500 comes from an eRASS1 count-rate-to-mass scaling relation; Fgas500 and R500 follow from those. They are NOT direct observations. The directly measured quantities are the count rates (CR*), counts (CTS*) and fluxes (F*).",
